{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538952115,"sessionID":"ses_e2d24d448ffeIzsz4Jpv5g585w","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2db544e001u15XssKV6pSMoO","sessionID":"ses_e2d24d448ffeIzsz4Jpv5g585w","messageID":"msg_1d2db425b001JzUkyZPQsVJQGp","type":"tool","id":"call_5379450d80e947a28bb41d20","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,80p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\"\ndescription: \"Ordered single-change tasks, grouped in waves of disjoint files, that measure the embedder's cost, make its state visible, add the plan-first doctor route, bound the prompt embedding and write the install guides.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"embedder setup and cost tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`. `S` is this packet's `scratch/` folder. `X` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. `E` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`. `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer'`. `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`. `R` is the phase 002 rollup query over `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, as `../002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/tasks.md` T026 writes it. `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`.\n\nEach task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. No task reads holdout prompt text. The captures report holdout counts only. No task installs Ollama, pulls or deletes a model, or starts or stops the server. The values below follow the operator's answers of 2026-11-12 recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n\nWorker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n- Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005. Read-only setup.\n- Wave 1: T006 (`E`), T007 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T008 (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), T009 (route workflow YAML), T010 (`skill-graph-db.ts`).\n- Wave 2: T011 (`E`), T012 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T013 (`advisor-status.ts`), T014 (`_routes.yaml`), T015 (skill-advisor presentation).\n- Wave 3: T016 (`E`), T017 (`advisor-status.ts`), T018 (`skill-advisor.md`), T019 (degrade test), T020 (`scoring-compatibility.json` and the files `D` regenerates).\n- Wave 4: T021 (`advisor-recommend.ts`), T022 (status test), T023 (`doctor-setup.yaml`), T024 (setup presentation), T025 (`doctor-install.yaml`), T026 (install presentation).\n- Wave 5: T027 (degrade test), T028 (route contract test), T029 (install contract test), T030 (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`), T031 (build and scan, no tracked file).\n- Then one at a time: T032 to T036, then T037 to T044.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, tune combined 9 of 45, holdout combined 0 of 44 and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`. `node $C --real-embedding | $M` prints tune combined 14 of 45 and holdout combined 2 of 44. `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n- [x] T002 Copy `../004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` to `$S/hook-latency.mjs` and run it three times (`$S/hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: `jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]'` on each file prints 44 and two numbers.\n- [x] T003 Record whether Ollama keeps loading the model after a client gives up (`$S/cold-after-abort.txt`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, then run `curl -s -m 0.05 localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{\"model\":\"nomic-embed-text:v1.5\",\"input\":\"x\"}'; sleep 3; curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq -r '.models[].name'`. Verify: the file holds the last command's output and one line saying whether it lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`.\n- [x] T004 Save every reader of the semantic lane health and of `disabledReason` (`$S/health-consumers.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"semanticLaneHealth|SemanticLaneHealth|disabledReason\" $ADV .skilled/commands/doctor --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' > $S/health-consumers.txt` exits 0 and each line is marked `reads`, `writes` or `test`.\n- [x] T005 Confirm phase 005 is merged before any edit to its files (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints at least one line. If it prints nothing, stop and report.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [x] T006 Create `E` with the server section only: read `/api/version`, `/api/tags` (the size of `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`) and `/api/ps` (loaded name, `size`, `size_vram` and `expires_at`) from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`, read `ps -axo pid,rss,command` for the `ollama serve` row and the model runner row (`llama-server` or `ollama runner`), print one JSON object and exit 2 with `ollama server not answering at <url>` on stderr when `/api/version` fails (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c 'keys'` lists the server keys and exits 0, and `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E` exits 2 and prints that message.\n- [x] T007 In `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, add `export const PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS = 750` and race `adapter.embed([prompt], { inputType: 'query' })` against a timer that rejects with an error named `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError`. Clear the timer in a `finally`, and attach `.catch(() => undefined)` to the embed promise so a late rejection is never unhandled (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0, in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed, and `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers.\n- [x] T008 Add two optional fields to the semantic lane health schema. `backend` is an object with `state` in `reachable`, `unreachable`, `model_missing` or `probe_not_implemented` and a nullable `reason` string. `commandVectorCoverage` is an object with non-negative integers `embedded` and `total`. Keep the schema `.strict()` (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `rg -n \"commandVectorCoverage|probe_not_implemented\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints two lines.\n- [x] T009 Create the route workflow. Phase 1 probes read-only: `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Phase 2 prints the plan through the presentation contract, one line per missing step with its cost from `node $E` or the install guide and its undo. Phase 3 asks for approval and stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` on anything but approve, or stops with `STATUS=OK` after the plan under `--dry-run`. Phase 4 runs only the approved steps: `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` and `ollama serve` in the background, while the Ollama install itself is only printed for the user to run. Phase 5 runs `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Phase 6 reruns the probe and renders the result, naming a daemon restart when `activeEmbedder` is null (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`). Verify: `python3 -c 'import sys,yaml; yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1]))' DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` exits 0 and `rg -n \"CANCELLED|dry_run|skill_graph_scan\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` prints at least three lines.\n- [x] T010 Export `readCommandEmbeddingSources` unchanged, so status can count the command entries that carry `embeddingText` (`$ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"^export function readCommandEmbeddingSources\" $ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` prints one line and `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0.\n- [x] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n- [x] T012 In the `catch` of `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, set `disabledReason` from the error that `adapter.embed` or the deadline raised: `prompt_embedding_model_missing` for `OllamaModelNotLoadedError`, `prompt_embedding_timeout` for `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError` or `OllamaRequestTimeoutError`, `prompt_embedding_unreachable` for any other `OllamaBackendUnreachableError` and `prompt_embedding_failed` otherwise. Leave the reasons set before the embed (`database_absent`, `adapter_unavailable`, `dim_mismatch`) as they are (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"prompt_embedding_(model_missing|timeout|unreachable)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` prints three lines and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed.\n- [x] T013 In `readSemanticLaneHealth`, add `commandVectorCoverage`: `embedded` counts rows of `commandVecTableNameForDim(activeDim)` when that table exists and 0 otherwise, and `total` is `readCommandEmbeddingSources()?.length ?? 0` (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n- [x] T014 Add the route to the manifest after `router-reach`: `command: /doctor:skill-advisor`, `target: embedder`, `yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, `setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]`, `allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]`, `mutating: mutates`, a `gate3_location` naming the advisor database and the user's Ollama model store, the `cli_commands` T009 runs and three or more `trigger_phrases` of three or more words, such as \"set up meaning matching\", \"install the local embedder\" and \"ollama is not running for the advisor\" (`DOC/_routes.yaml`). Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n- [x] T015 Add the embedder blocks to the presentation contract: the probe dashboard, the plan table with columns step, cost and undo, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n -i \"embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` prints at least five lines.\n- [x] T016 Add the CLI section to `E`: five `X advisor_recommend` calls with distinct prompts timed end to end, printed as `cli.ms` (all five) and `cli.medianMs` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.cli'` prints five numbers and a median, and `git status --short` shows no change made by the run.\n- [x] T017 In `handleAdvisorStatus`, when `includeSemanticHealth` is set and the active manifest's backend is `ollama`, await `probeOllamaModel(resolveOllamaBaseUrl(), <manifest ollamaName>, 500)` and merge `backend` into `semanticLaneHealth`: `reachable` when available, `model_missing` when the reason says the model is not loaded and `unreachable` otherwise. Set `laneEnabled` to false unless `reachable`. A non-Ollama backend gets `probe_not_implemented`. Keep `readAdvisorStatus` synchronous (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n- [x] T018 Add the `embedder` row to the execution target table and to the `argument-hint` line (`DOC/skill-advisor.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"embedder\" DOC/skill-advisor.md` prints at least two lines.\n- [x] T019 Create the degrade test with the adapter, the active pointer and the read-only database mocked, and `VITEST` stubbed to `false` inside each case. Six rows: warm answer scored with a cosine, cold answer at 300 ms scored with a cosine, absent server, missing model, an answer that never arrives, which returns inside `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS` plus 100 ms, and a failure that leaves the result equal to the no-embedder result. Each failure row checks its `disabledReason` (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 6 passed.\n- [x] T020 Add the route's activation entry to both the `typescript` and the `python` lists, copying the shape of the `command-doctor-skill-advisor-router-reach` entries, then run `node $D` (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`). Verify: `node $D --check` prints `\"status\": \"fresh\"` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n- [x] T021 Add `export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[]`, which returns a one-item array holding `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` for a reason and an empty array for null, and call it in `outputWarnings` with `getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason` read right after the scored call (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers` reports 0 failed.\n- [x] T022 Add status cases with fixture databases: `commandVectorCoverage` with and without a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table, and `backend` for reachable, unreachable and model missing with `probeOllamaModel` mocked (`$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and at least five more passed than before.\n- [x] T023 Add the sixth leg after the advisor leg: run `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only`. PASS when `laneEnabled` is true and `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above 0. DEGRADED otherwise, never FAIL, with repair `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg. Change \"five read-only legs\" to \"six\" in the file (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"Leg embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"five read-only\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints nothing.\n- [x] T024 Add the `embedder` leg row to the per-leg table and the `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` row to the target list (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` prints at least two lines.\n- [x] T025 In the checklist sentence, insert \"5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install\" before the `/doctor:setup` step, and renumber that step to 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line.\n- [x] T026 In the printed checklist block, insert step `5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]` with the line \"Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\" and renumber `/doctor:setup` to step 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"^5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder|^6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` prints two lines.\n- [x] T027 Add a seventh row to the degrade test: `semanticLaneOffWarning` returns `[\"semantic_lane_off:prompt_embedding_unreachable\"]` for that reason and `[]` for null (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\"\ndescription: \"Ordered single-change tasks, grouped in waves of disjoint files, that measure the embedder's cost, make its state visible, add the plan-first doctor route, bound the prompt embedding and write the install guides.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"embedder setup and cost tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nEvery command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`. `S` is this packet's `scratch/` folder. `X` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. `E` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`. `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer'`. `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`. `R` is the phase 002 rollup query over `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, as `../002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/tasks.md` T026 writes it. `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`.\n\nEach task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. No task reads holdout prompt text. The captures report holdout counts only. No task installs Ollama, pulls or deletes a model, or starts or stops the server. The values below follow the operator's answers of 2026-11-12 recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n\nWorker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n- Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005. Read-only setup.\n- Wave 1: T006 (`E`), T007 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T008 (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), T009 (route workflow YAML), T010 (`skill-graph-db.ts`).\n- Wave 2: T011 (`E`), T012 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T013 (`advisor-status.ts`), T014 (`_routes.yaml`), T015 (skill-advisor presentation).\n- Wave 3: T016 (`E`), T017 (`advisor-status.ts`), T018 (`skill-advisor.md`), T019 (degrade test), T020 (`scoring-compatibility.json` and the files `D` regenerates).\n- Wave 4: T021 (`advisor-recommend.ts`), T022 (status test), T023 (`doctor-setup.yaml`), T024 (setup presentation), T025 (`doctor-install.yaml`), T026 (install presentation).\n- Wave 5: T027 (degrade test), T028 (route contract test), T029 (install contract test), T030 (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`), T031 (build and scan, no tracked file).\n- Then one at a time: T032 to T036, then T037 to T044.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, tune combined 9 of 45, holdout combined 0 of 44 and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`. `node $C --real-embedding | $M` prints tune combined 14 of 45 and holdout combined 2 of 44. `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n- [x] T002 Copy `../004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` to `$S/hook-latency.mjs` and run it three times (`$S/hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: `jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]'` on each file prints 44 and two numbers.\n- [x] T003 Record whether Ollama keeps loading the model after a client gives up (`$S/cold-after-abort.txt`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, then run `curl -s -m 0.05 localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{\"model\":\"nomic-embed-text:v1.5\",\"input\":\"x\"}'; sleep 3; curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq -r '.models[].name'`. Verify: the file holds the last command's output and one line saying whether it lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`.\n- [x] T004 Save every reader of the semantic lane health and of `disabledReason` (`$S/health-consumers.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"semanticLaneHealth|SemanticLaneHealth|disabledReason\" $ADV .skilled/commands/doctor --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' > $S/health-consumers.txt` exits 0 and each line is marked `reads`, `writes` or `test`.\n- [x] T005 Confirm phase 005 is merged before any edit to its files (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints at least one line. If it prints nothing, stop and report.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [x] T006 Create `E` with the server section only: read `/api/version`, `/api/tags` (the size of `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`) and `/api/ps` (loaded name, `size`, `size_vram` and `expires_at`) from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`, read `ps -axo pid,rss,command` for the `ollama serve` row and the model runner row (`llama-server` or `ollama runner`), print one JSON object and exit 2 with `ollama server not answering at <url>` on stderr when `/api/version` fails (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c 'keys'` lists the server keys and exits 0, and `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E` exits 2 and prints that message.\n- [x] T007 In `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, add `export const PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS = 750` and race `adapter.embed([prompt], { inputType: 'query' })` against a timer that rejects with an error named `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError`. Clear the timer in a `finally`, and attach `.catch(() => undefined)` to the embed promise so a late rejection is never unhandled (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0, in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed, and `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers.\n- [x] T008 Add two optional fields to the semantic lane health schema. `backend` is an object with `state` in `reachable`, `unreachable`, `model_missing` or `probe_not_implemented` and a nullable `reason` string. `commandVectorCoverage` is an object with non-negative integers `embedded` and `total`. Keep the schema `.strict()` (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `rg -n \"commandVectorCoverage|probe_not_implemented\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints two lines.\n- [x] T009 Create the route workflow. Phase 1 probes read-only: `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Phase 2 prints the plan through the presentation contract, one line per missing step with its cost from `node $E` or the install guide and its undo. Phase 3 asks for approval and stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` on anything but approve, or stops with `STATUS=OK` after the plan under `--dry-run`. Phase 4 runs only the approved steps: `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` and `ollama serve` in the background, while the Ollama install itself is only printed for the user to run. Phase 5 runs `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Phase 6 reruns the probe and renders the result, naming a daemon restart when `activeEmbedder` is null (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`). Verify: `python3 -c 'import sys,yaml; yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1]))' DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` exits 0 and `rg -n \"CANCELLED|dry_run|skill_graph_scan\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` prints at least three lines.\n- [x] T010 Export `readCommandEmbeddingSources` unchanged, so status can count the command entries that carry `embeddingText` (`$ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"^export function readCommandEmbeddingSources\" $ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` prints one line and `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0.\n- [x] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n- [x] T012 In the `catch` of `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, set `disabledReason` from the error that `adapter.embed` or the deadline raised: `prompt_embedding_model_missing` for `OllamaModelNotLoadedError`, `prompt_embedding_timeout` for `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError` or `OllamaRequestTimeoutError`, `prompt_embedding_unreachable` for any other `OllamaBackendUnreachableError` and `prompt_embedding_failed` otherwise. Leave the reasons set before the embed (`database_absent`, `adapter_unavailable`, `dim_mismatch`) as they are (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"prompt_embedding_(model_missing|timeout|unreachable)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` prints three lines and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed.\n- [x] T013 In `readSemanticLaneHealth`, add `commandVectorCoverage`: `embedded` counts rows of `commandVecTableNameForDim(activeDim)` when that table exists and 0 otherwise, and `total` is `readCommandEmbeddingSources()?.length ?? 0` (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n- [x] T014 Add the route to the manifest after `router-reach`: `command: /doctor:skill-advisor`, `target: embedder`, `yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, `setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]`, `allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]`, `mutating: mutates`, a `gate3_location` naming the advisor database and the user's Ollama model store, the `cli_commands` T009 runs and three or more `trigger_phrases` of three or more words, such as \"set up meaning matching\", \"install the local embedder\" and \"ollama is not running for the advisor\" (`DOC/_routes.yaml`). Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n- [x] T015 Add the embedder blocks to the presentation contract: the probe dashboard, the plan table with columns step, cost and undo, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n -i \"embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` prints at least five lines.\n- [x] T016 Add the CLI section to `E`: five `X advisor_recommend` calls with distinct prompts timed end to end, printed as `cli.ms` (all five) and `cli.medianMs` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.cli'` prints five numbers and a median, and `git status --short` shows no change made by the run.\n- [x] T017 In `handleAdvisorStatus`, when `includeSemanticHealth` is set and the active manifest's backend is `ollama`, await `probeOllamaModel(resolveOllamaBaseUrl(), <manifest ollamaName>, 500)` and merge `backend` into `semanticLaneHealth`: `reachable` when available, `model_missing` when the reason says the model is not loaded and `unreachable` otherwise. Set `laneEnabled` to false unless `reachable`. A non-Ollama backend gets `probe_not_implemented`. Keep `readAdvisorStatus` synchronous (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n- [x] T018 Add the `embedder` row to the execution target table and to the `argument-hint` line (`DOC/skill-advisor.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"embedder\" DOC/skill-advisor.md` prints at least two lines.\n- [x] T019 Create the degrade test with the adapter, the active pointer and the read-only database mocked, and `VITEST` stubbed to `false` inside each case. Six rows: warm answer scored with a cosine, cold answer at 300 ms scored with a cosine, absent server, missing model, an answer that never arrives, which returns inside `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS` plus 100 ms, and a failure that leaves the result equal to the no-embedder result. Each failure row checks its `disabledReason` (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 6 passed.\n- [x] T020 Add the route's activation entry to both the `typescript` and the `python` lists, copying the shape of the `command-doctor-skill-advisor-router-reach` entries, then run `node $D` (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`). Verify: `node $D --check` prints `\"status\": \"fresh\"` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n- [x] T021 Add `export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[]`, which returns a one-item array holding `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` for a reason and an empty array for null, and call it in `outputWarnings` with `getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason` read right after the scored call (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers` reports 0 failed.\n- [x] T022 Add status cases with fixture databases: `commandVectorCoverage` with and without a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table, and `backend` for reachable, unreachable and model missing with `probeOllamaModel` mocked (`$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and at least five more passed than before.\n- [x] T023 Add the sixth leg after the advisor leg: run `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only`. PASS when `laneEnabled` is true and `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above 0. DEGRADED otherwise, never FAIL, with repair `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg. Change \"five read-only legs\" to \"six\" in the file (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"Leg embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"five read-only\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints nothing.\n- [x] T024 Add the `embedder` leg row to the per-leg table and the `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` row to the target list (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` prints at least two lines.\n- [x] T025 In the checklist sentence, insert \"5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install\" before the `/doctor:setup` step, and renumber that step to 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line.\n- [x] T026 In the printed checklist block, insert step `5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]` with the line \"Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\" and renumber `/doctor:setup` to step 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"^5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder|^6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` prints two lines.\n- [x] T027 Add a seventh row to the degrade test: `semanticLaneOffWarning` returns `[\"semantic_lane_off:prompt_embedding_unreachable\"]` for that reason and `[]` for null (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '1,80p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538951758,"end":1794538952115}}}}
