` | 768 | `ollama` | `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 5000 | 768-dim retrieval specialist. Local-first cascade default per ADR-014. Uses `search_query: ` / `search_document: ` prefix tokens. |\n301: | `mxbai-embed-large-v1` | 1024 | `ollama` | `mxbai-embed-large:latest` | 1200 | Phase `016/004` paraphrase-strong candidate. |\n302: | `bge-small-en-v1.5` | 384 | `ollama` | `bge-small-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | Compact 33M-param baseline. |\n303: | `bge-large-en-v1.5` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-large-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | BAAI flagship retrieval model. |\n304: | `jina-embeddings-v3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `hf.co/gaianet/jina-embeddings-v3-GGUF:Q4_K_M` | 8000 | Multilingual + paraphrase-tuned. Matryoshka representation allows 256 / 512 / 768 / 1024 truncation. |\n305: | `bge-m3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-m3:latest` | 8000 | Multilingual hybrid (dense + sparse + colbert). |\n306: | `snowflake-arctic-embed-l-v2.0` | 1024 | `ollama` | `snowflake-arctic-embed2:latest` | 8000 | Snowflake late-2024 flagship. 8192 context, multilingual, top MTEB retrieval scores. |\n307: \n308: > **Content-type split.** The TS shared registry is text-tuned by design. The `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter on the shared cascade preserves the conceptual split for any future TS code consumer. The previous skill-advisor-specific `jina-embeddings-v2-base-code` entry was removed because it was code-tuned and did not belong in a text-only registry.\n309: \n310: Adding a new candidate is a single registry row in the shared package plus, if the backend is new, a single adapter under `shared/embeddings/adapters/`. No call sites change. The adapter contract (`EmbedderAdapter` in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapter.ts`) is small — `embed()` plus `ready()`.\n311: \n312: ### 12.3 Swap mechanism: `'auto'` sentinel + `setActiveEmbedder()`\n313: \n314: There are two operator-facing surfaces. **Neither is an environment variable.**\n315: \n316: **Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n317: \n318: **Manual override.** [`setActiveEmbedder()`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts) writes a specific manifest into `vec_metadata` and creates the matching `vec_<dim>` table:\n319: \n320: ```typescript\n321: import Database from 'better-sqlite3';\n322: import { setActiveEmbedder } from './runtime/dist/.../lib/embedders/schema.js';\n323: \n324: const db = new Database('.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite');\n325: setActiveEmbedder(db, 'jina-embeddings-v3', 1024);\n326: ```\n327: \n328: Effect of the call:\n329: \n330: - `vec_metadata.active_embedder_name` -> `jina-embeddings-v3`\n331: - `vec_metadata.active_embedder_dim` -> `1024`\n332: - `vec_1024` table created (if absent), schema `(skill_id, embedding BLOB, model_id, content_hash, updated_at)`\n333: - `hasActiveEmbedderPointer(db)` returns `true`, so both read path (`semantic-shadow.ts`, `loadSkillEmbeddings()`) and write path (`refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter`) target `vec_<active.dim>`\n334: - The shared cascade is skipped on subsequent restarts (a manual override pins the pointer)\n335: \n336: There are intentionally no embedder-administration commands here. Skill-advisor's surface is one database helper plus the cascade-driven sentinel. Operator discipline owns any manual swap workflow; there is no async re-index orchestrator on the skill-advisor side.\n337: \n338: ### 12.4 Operator-safe swap runbook\n339: \n340: The writer cross-wire shipped in phase `004` and the cascade-driven default shipped in phase `003/006`. The pointer flip is now safe end-to-end:\n341: \n342: 1. Stop the daemon.\n343: 2. Snapshot `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`.\n344: 3. (Optional) Call `setActiveEmbedder()` to override the cascade choice.\n345: 4. Restart the daemon. `ensureActiveEmbedder()` either honours your override or runs the cascade. The first scan or watcher tick populates `vec_<active.dim>` via the adapter dispatcher.\n346: 5. Smoke-test `advisor_recommend` through the CLI against three queries (`\"memory save\"`, `\"code search\"`, `\"spec folder\"`) and confirm top-3 picks are sane.\n347: \n348: The full runbook (snapshot + stop + override + restart + smoke test + rollback) is documented at [`002-jina-swap-and-reindex/evidence/swap-runbook.md`](../../<spec-folder>). The \"Architecture Context\" and \"Half-wired state\" sections are now historical — the half-wired state was closed by phase `004`.\n349: \n350: ### 12.5 Device selection\n351: \n352: Skill-advisor does not ship an explicit `_resolve_device()` shim. Device selection inherits from the underlying backend:\n353: \n354: | Backend | Device handling |\n355: | --- | --- |\n356: | `ollama` (default after cascade picks tier 1) | Ollama owns runtime device handling. It already covers Metal / CUDA / CPU autonomously based on its own daemon configuration. |\n357: | `hf-local` (fallback tier 2) | Pure-Node `@huggingface/transformers` HTTP model server (zero Python). Device handling (MPS / CUDA / CPU) is resolved by the model server's own runtime. |\n358: | `api` (OpenAI or Voyage fallback) | Remote inference; device handling is the provider's concern. |\n359: \n360: If you need MPS-style auto-detect for a local model, the Ollama backend already provides it on Apple Silicon by default — install Ollama, pull a manifest, the cascade picks it.\n361: \n362: ### 12.6 Cross-references\n363: \n364: - Canonical shared-embedder narrative: [`embedder-pluggability.md`](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md) — covers skill-advisor and the shared design rationale.\n365: - Shared contract surface: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/) — the canonical adapter, types, registry and Ollama adapter.\n366: - Shared cascade: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/auto-select.ts) — file-locked Ollama → hf-local → OpenAI → Voyage probe chain (ADR-014 local-first). Accepts optional `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter (default `'text'`).\n367: - Skill-advisor schema helpers: [`runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts).\n368: - Architecture-gap follow-on: packet `003/006-shared-embedder-logic-with-spec-memory` (shipped phase 003/006).\n369: \n370: ### 12.7 Setup route and cost\n371: \n372: `/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost.\n373: \n374: What the embedder costs on this machine, measured 2026-11-13 with `runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`:\n375: \n376: | Measure | Value |\n377: | --- | ---: |\n378: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes (261.6 MiB) |\n379: | Idle memory, `ollama serve` with no model loaded | 25776 KB (25.2 MiB) |\n380: | Loaded memory, model runner resident | 279520 KB (273.0 MiB) |\n381: | Unload after the last call | 5 minutes, Ollama keep-alive |\n382: | Warm embed latency, model loaded | 4.8 ms median, 8.9 ms p95 |\n383: | Cold first call after the unload | 538.53 ms |\n384: \n385: Once the approved steps ran, the route runs `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. That scan is what writes the command vectors into the `vec_cmd_<dim>` table: without it `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` stays at zero and the semantic lane reports off. The database is derived state and gitignored, since `.gitignore` ignores `runtime/database/*.sqlite`, so the scan costs its own runtime plus the warm latency per embedded prompt and leaves nothing for git.\n386: \n387: ---\n388: \n389: ## 13. RELATED RESOURCES\n390: \n391: | Document | Purpose |\n392: | --- | --- |\n393: | [README.md](./README.md) | Operator overview, quick start, runtime integrations. |\n394: | [ARCHITECTURE.md](./ARCHITECTURE.md) | Package-local architecture and public API entrypoints. |\n395: | [Hook reference](./hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md) | Prompt-time hook surfaces for each runtime. |\n396: | [Manual testing playbook](./manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md) | OP-001 / OP-002 operator scenarios + indexer edge cases. |\n397: | [Embedder pluggability narrative](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md) | Canonical embedder-pluggability reference. |\n398: \n399: ---\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 400]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md\",\"offset\":270,\"limit\":130}"},"time":{"start":1794538964658,"end":1794538965232}}}}
