{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539017037,"sessionID":"ses_e2d24d448ffeIzsz4Jpv5g585w","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2dc4f45001RnYts7LZrbIY2M","sessionID":"ses_e2d24d448ffeIzsz4Jpv5g585w","messageID":"msg_1d2dc3ef9001AoXu7PHqFYErta","type":"tool","id":"call_f244d39e265e4f1e93215320","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"includeEmbeddingsHealth\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md; echo \"exit=$?\""},"output":"372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\nexit=0\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"372:`/doctor:install` includes the embedder setup by default, and the setup itself runs as `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from inside the target repo. The route probes `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `advisor_status --include-semantic-health true`, prints one plan row per missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks once before it runs anything. A no stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` and changes nothing. `--dry-run` prints the plan and stops with `STATUS=OK`. The route never installs or upgrades Ollama: it prints the install command for the operator, and the install guide owns that cost. The two health flags split the diagnosis: `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes only the hf-local model server, while `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder and probes its backend.\nexit=0\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"includeEmbeddingsHealth\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539016005,"end":1794539017037}}}}
